\section{Reproducibility and independent streams}{

Every sequence is a deterministic function of a single seed (or of a stream
that is handed to the call). The modules of one call draw from independent
L'Ecuyer-CMRG sub-streams derived from that seed, so the modules are
independent and a call to \code{\link{smr_alloc}} never changes the random
number state of the calling session. For high-frequency calling,
\code{\link{smr_streams}} derives a family of non-overlapping sub-streams
from one base seed; handing one stream to each call guarantees that no two
calls ever draw from the same random numbers, so a loop stays both
reproducible and free of repeated streams.
}

\section{Confidentiality}{

ICH E9 and good clinical practice require the block structure and the seed to
remain confidential. \code{keep.blocks = FALSE} drops the block columns from
\code{$alloc} and from every exported artefact, while the statistician's
copy of the structure stays available in \code{$blocks} for quality control.
}

